{
 "what": "Schematic 3D body plans. A frame places the parts of a blueprint in space so a person can click a wing, a leg or an eye in the theatre view and be shown what constrains it.",
 "contract_version": "0.11.0",
 "geometry_basis": "schematic",
 "THIS_IS_NOT_MORPHOMETRY": "Every position here is DECLARED by this file, not measured from any specimen and not derived from any ontology. A slot says 'the eye goes near the front of the head, on both sides'; it does not say how big a fly's eye is or where it sits in millimetres. The only morphometric geometry in this repository is anatomy-model/parametric, which builds one teleost from Park and Choi's measurements. Nothing here should ever be read off as a measurement, and the theatre view labels every part with this basis.",
 "why_it_is_still_worth_having": "The alternative is the radial hierarchy the live page already draws, where a wing and a gonad are two dots at the same radius because both are organs. A schematic body is wrong about dimensions and right about adjacency, and adjacency is what a person needs to click the thing they mean.",
 "axes": {
  "x": "anterior (+) to posterior (-), normalised to the body's own length",
  "y": "dorsal (+) to ventral (-)",
  "z": "right (+) to left (-); a slot with side \"paired\" is instantiated at +z and -z",
  "units": "body lengths, so a frame is scale-free"
 },
 "matching": {
  "order": "uberon id first, then label pattern, then the parent's slot, then unplaced",
  "unplaced": "A part that matches no slot is NOT placed at the origin. It is returned in `unplaced` with its level and label, and the theatre lists it beside the body. A silently mispositioned part is worse than an absent one.",
  "patterns": "Label patterns are matched case-insensitively against the ontology label the blueprint carries, which came from Uberon or CL. They are deliberately broad: `matched_by` records which rule fired for every part so a wrong placement can be traced to one line of this file."
 },
